statement:
Let $\mathbb{N}$ denote the set of all positive integers. Find all real numbers $c$ for which there exists a function $f : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ satisfying:
\begin{itemize}
\item for any $x, a \in \mathbb{N}$, the quantity $\dfrac{f(x+a) - f(x)}{a}$ is an integer if and only if $a = 1$;
\item for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$, we have $|f(x) - cx| < 2023$.
\end{itemize}
